flowchart LR
  %% QUESTION THIS DIAGRAM ANSWERS: competitive bidding is the general rule. Which other modes does the law allow, and for what kind of situation is each one meant?
  %% READING: left = the kind of situation. Right = the mode. The order of the modes follows sections 26 to 37 of the Act.
  %% SOURCES: the names and the number of the modes are verified in the Act [RA12009 ss.26-37]. The mode must be stated in the Annual Procurement Plan [RA12009 s.7]. The conditions and amounts of modes 2 to 9 are from sections 28 to 35 of the Implementing Rules, read in October 2026 [IRR12009]. The committee for bids may delegate modes 5 to 11 to the end-user unit or the procurement unit [IRR12009 s.26].
  %% NOT READ: the copy of the Implementing Rules that I could open ends inside section 35.5. The cases of negotiated procurement after the fifth case, and sections 36 and 37, were not read. The descriptions of modes 10 and 11 are from general knowledge. The lines give the main condition only. Do not rely on this diagram for a legal decision on the mode.

  S(["One line of the<br/>Annual Procurement Plan"]) --> Q{"What is the<br/>situation?"}

  Q -- "general rule" --> M1["1  COMPETITIVE BIDDING<br/>open to all eligible bidders (see 06b)"]:::main
  Q -- "few known suppliers of a<br/>specialized item" --> M2["2  LIMITED SOURCE BIDDING<br/>invitation to pre-selected suppliers: highly specialized goods or<br/>consulting from few sources, major plant components,<br/>specialized works that affect national security"]
  Q -- "the agency cannot yet<br/>define the solution" --> M3["3  COMPETITIVE DIALOGUE<br/>two stages, for innovative or complex needs and for<br/>specifications that cannot be defined in advance"]
  Q -- "a private party offers a<br/>new concept or technology" --> M4["4  UNSOLICITED OFFER WITH BID MATCHING<br/>the agency invites competing bids, and the<br/>first offeror may match the best one"]
  Q -- "only one source exists" --> M5["5  DIRECT CONTRACTING<br/>goods only: proprietary item, critical component from one<br/>source, or exclusive dealer with no cheaper sub-dealer"]
  Q -- "readily available item<br/>of small amount" --> M6["6  DIRECT ACQUISITION<br/>contract budget up to PHP 200,000, from a registered<br/>supplier, an online shop or an item sold ready for use"]
  Q -- "more of the same item from<br/>the last winning bidder" --> M7["7  REPEAT ORDER<br/>same or lower unit price, within 6 months of the notice to<br/>proceed, at most 25 percent of the first quantity"]
  Q -- "amount below a threshold" --> M8["8  SMALL VALUE PROCUREMENT<br/>contract budget up to PHP 2,000,000 (lower for smaller local<br/>governments, PHP 100,000 for a barangay). Request for quotations"]
  Q -- "failed biddings, emergency,<br/>and other listed cases" --> M9["9  NEGOTIATED PROCUREMENT<br/>listed cases, among them: two failed biddings, emergency,<br/>take-over of an ended contract, adjacent work, another agency"]
  Q -- "the supplier already sold the<br/>same item to the government" --> M10["10  DIRECT SALES<br/>same item, same or lower price"]
  Q -- "research, development<br/>and innovation needs" --> M11["11  DIRECT PROCUREMENT FOR SCIENCE,<br/>TECHNOLOGY AND INNOVATION"]

